104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (Traditional,hand-writtensoftware engineering demands mastery across a deep and unforgiving technical stack. At the application layer, engineers must manage memory allocation and lifecycle \(or, in managed runtimes, understand garbage-collection behavior well enough to avoid leaks and latency spikes\). At the data layer, teams perform manual database schema migrations, carefully versioning structural changes to avoid data loss or downtime in production systems. At the integration layer, engineers implement API security protocols such as OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect \(OIDC\) to govern authentication and authorization between services. Delivery itself is industrialized through CI/CD pipelines built on tools such as GitHub Actions or Jenkins, and applications are packaged and orchestrated using containerization technologies such as Docker and Kubernetes. Each of these disciplines is itself a specialization, and enterprise-grade software typically requires competence in all of them simultaneously. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
